    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d217">

                <pb facs="d216-3" n="3" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v03mSupp/d216-3"/>

                <head>217. Telegram 6 from Geneva to Hong Kong<anchor n="1" xml:id="d217-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Geneva</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1955-09-22">September 22, 1955,
                        noon</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d217-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d217-1"/>
                <p>6. Would appreciate any immediately available information whether nine jailed
                    Americans released from Communist China were informed by prison officials of
                    these negotiations or terms of agreed announcement before their release.
                        Wang has alleged remaining <pb
                        facs="0334" n="287" type="typeset" xml:id="pg287"/> prisoners will be
                    informed agreed announcement by having newspapers read and if necessary
                    translated to them.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Shillock</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
